From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dubzer <me@dubzer.dev>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 18:17:25 +0300
Subject: Open attachment photos with a smaller preview first

Use smaller photo previews when opening attachments to reduce decoding,
resizing and texture-upload work. Request the normal full-size viewer
image once the current photo settles after opening or swiping, or right
away when the user starts editing, keeping the preview visible until it
is ready and deferring editing until loading completes.

Preserve zoom through asynchronous image replacement, retain already
edited bitmaps, and clear preview state when the photo changes or the
viewer closes or is destroyed.
